<title>ESTONIA: HANSA LEASING TO ISSUE TWO-YEAR BONDS.</title>
<headline>HANSA LEASING TO ISSUE TWO-YEAR BONDS.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hansa Leasing, the subsidiary of Hansapank, is to issue two-year bonds worth 85 million kroons next week, Hansapank said on Monday.</p>
<p>The coupon is 10.25 percent and the bonds will be sold at 99.50 percent, Ulo Kallas, Hansapank interest rate products manager, told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;They are using it to refinance their previous liabilities as bonds are cheaper,&quot; Kallas said.</p>
<p>Hansa Leasing on Tuesday issued new six-month commercial paper worth 30 million kroons with a yield of 8.5 percent.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
